# CODEOWNERS — auto-requested reviewers per path.
#
# HOW THIS WORKS:
#   When a PR touches a path listed below, GitHub automatically requests
#   a review from the listed owner (team or user). The PR can still be
#   merged if (a) the owner approves, or (b) the merger is in a group
#   configured to bypass CODEOWNERS in repo Settings → Branches →
#   "Allow specified actors to bypass pull request requirements".
#
# PERMISSIONS MODEL (recommended):
#   * Admins / Maintainers  → bypass CODEOWNERS via repo settings.
#                                They can merge freely without per-path
#                                reviews.
#   * Team members           → cannot bypass. Their PRs must collect the
#                                listed owner's review before merge.
#
# SUBSTITUTION: forks replace `@morvenlabs` with their own user or team
# handles (e.g. `@your-org/maintainers`). Unknown owners are ignored
# by GitHub and flagged as errors in the CODEOWNERS file view.

# Default: no global owner. Most paths have no CODEOWNERS requirement,
# so non-listed paths merge without a forced reviewer (admins do).

# ─── CI/CD & release infra ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Touching workflows or release config is risky — require maintainer
# sign-off on every PR.
.github/                   @morvenlabs
/release.config.mjs         @morvenlabs

# ─── Backend ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# API code and the shared Prisma schema need backend-review.
/apps/api/                  @morvenlabs
/packages/db/               @morvenlabs

# ─── Frontend ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Next.js / shadcn code needs frontend-review.
/apps/web/                  @morvenlabs

# ─── Shared types ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Both backend and frontend consume this package — list both reviewers.
/packages/shared-types/     @morvenlabs
